The instrument loggers (``self.log`` and ``self.visa_log`` of instruments, channels and other
instrument modules) no longer log while the garbage collector closes an instrument that was not
closed, since the garbage collector runs at an arbitrary point in time and on any thread, possibly
in the middle of other logging, where logging is not safe with all log handlers.
``IPInstrument`` now logs through its instrument logger, so that this also applies to it. Its log
records are therefore emitted by the ``qcodes.instrument.instrument_base`` logger with the name of
the instrument, rather than by the ``qcodes.instrument.ip`` logger.
